From 059b61d79f9fc66276979fff2e3abb5519d5d304 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 12:51:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 248/249] patch 0248 -- gus-5 (#41 latent-H1): arm _playing
 AFTER on_song_start

The GUS MidiBackendGus::on_song_start() uploads GM .pat instruments to GF1
DRAM via slow byte-wise PIO pokes, in main-loop context. MidiScheduler::start()
previously set _playing=true BEFORE calling on_song_start(), so the PIT music
pump's tick_isr (a real INT8 hardware IRQ on DOS) could preempt mid-upload and
dispatch a note into a half-uploaded instrument bank -- a voice contending the
card during the poke window.

Move _playing=true to AFTER on_song_start() returns. The pump cannot dispatch
any note until every instrument is resident. Backends with a no-op
on_song_start (SB/OPL) are unaffected; the only added latency is the upload
time, already synchronous in start().

Latent-risk close for gus-5; the gus-4b music hang itself is the SDL-side PIO
poke (sdl-pg autoinc fix), not this dispatch race.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp b/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp
index ba0f23b8..56c13acb 100644
--- a/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp
@@ -350,12 +350,26 @@ void MidiScheduler::start()
     _last_tick_now_ms = 0;  // first tick() sets this; treats first delta as 0
     _tempo_us_per_quarter = 500000;  // reset to SMF default; tempo events re-set
     _recompute_us_per_tick();
-    _playing = true;
+    // patch 0248 (gus-5, latent-H1 close): _playing is armed AFTER on_song_-
+    // start() below, NOT here. The GUS backend's on_song_start() uploads .pat
+    // instruments via slow PIO pokes in main-loop context; were _playing true
+    // now, the PIT music pump's tick_isr could preempt mid-upload and dispatch
+    // a note into a half-uploaded instrument bank. Arming after the uploads
+    // complete means the pump cannot dispatch until every instrument is
+    // resident. Backends whose on_song_start is a no-op (SB/OPL) are
+    // unaffected -- the only added latency is the upload time itself.
   }
   if (_backend)
   {
     _backend->on_song_start();
   }
+  // Arm playback now that the backend has finished any per-song setup (GUS
+  // .pat uploads). cli/sti so the ISR sees the flip atomically vs the state
+  // reset above.
+  {
+    MidiIsrCriticalSection _cs;
+    _playing = true;
+  }
 }
 
 void MidiScheduler::stop()
